			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://phpc.social/@andrewfeeney\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>andrewfeeney</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Well I can't read it. 🤷🏻‍♂️</p><p>I'll happily cop to being cognitively impared so that utility-classes-gone-wild can be seen as an accessibility violation. If all of this were in a co-located &lt;style&gt; tag as vanilla CSS, I could read that easily. 😊</p>",
