		{
			"id": "112100100298413704",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti/112100100235962086",
			"author": {
				"name": "thurti",
				"url": "https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/314/593/032/380/929/original/8a60fd575ce8ed01.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-15T14:09:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> When did this actually start, that developers here have become so passive aggressive and condescending towards the work of other developers. I thought it was just a twitter thing.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112100214465796095",
			"parentId": "112100100298413704",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112100214465796095",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-15T14:38:46.396Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.anoxinon.de/@thurti\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>thurti</span></a></span> I think there is a lot to unpack here and I don’t go into making this joke without self awareness of what’s happening.</p><p>But I would ask: when did tooling tribalism become so that we can’t critique code? That a mere lighthearted humorous critique of code is a personal attack?</p><p>Finally the thing I always try to evaluate before making a joke like this: is it punching down? And no, I would very strongly argue that it is not.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
